{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`**\n1. The SDK passes the requested path and selector to `Domain::source_node`.\n2. When the domain returns `NodeData`, the SDK interns it in the domain cache to get a `NodeId<Self>`.\n3. When the domain returns an error for an unsupported or invalid address, the SDK surfaces the error.\n\n**Coverage by the marked tests**\n- `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` covers all three obligations.\n  - Its `Project` fixture returns an error for `unknown.txt` and for the selector `line[unknown]`. The test reads both addresses through `ValidationContext::read_source`, so both the path and the selector must have been forwarded unchanged.\n  - Each read must fail with the mapping error (\"unsupported source item\"). No dependency is recorded, and `node_content` is never called (`reads == 0`).\n  - A valid address (`source.txt` with an empty selector) returns `NodeData` `\"source-node\"`. The test asserts that the dependency is `intern_node(\"source-node\")` with the returned fingerprint, and that the content read was for `\"source-node\"`. This shows the data is interned into a `NodeId`. The `fail_read` step also checks that a later read error is kept separate from the mapping errors.\n- `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` covers the production tool paths (`list_sources` and `search_text` hits).\n  - Its `TestDomain::source_node` records each `OutlineData` it receives. The test asserts that the recorded address is exactly `visible/selected.txt` with an empty selector.\n  - It asserts that the answer's dependencies are the interned `TestNode` ids 7, 8, 9 and 10, the ids that `TestDomain::source_node` returns for the selected, alpha, beta and unused files. Each of these goes through `source_node` and then `intern_node`.\n  - It repeats the run twice.\n- `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` only checks the exported API inventory. It adds nothing behavioural, but it does no harm.\n\n**Possible gaps considered, and why I did not report them**\n- The marked tests never read a non-empty selector successfully. Selector forwarding is still shown by the `line[unknown]` error case. The tool paths that build an `OutlineData` copy the selector without changing it, so a different selector would not need different handling.\n- The default `Domain::source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`. `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` asserts this but is not marked with a `{test}` reference to this requirement. The requirement's \"unsupported address returns an error\" obligation is carried by the domain, and the SDK-side propagation is asserted by the marked tests. I treat the missing marker as a minor point. It is not enough to call the tests inadequate.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behaviour that the marked tests would accept.",
  "references": "f2a80deb786be0869fd8f9959f206506d5e92b0c12b7cd54d96c008cea83d3f0",
